      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nThe `runtime.v1` gRPC server (`rust/sglang-grpc`) hands a plain `TcpListener` to tonic through\r\n`serve_with_incoming_shutdown`. tonic applies its `tcp_nodelay` setting only to listeners it binds itself, so the\r\nsockets this server accepts keep Nagle's algorithm enabled. Streamed responses are one small frame per token, all\r\nflowing server → client with almost nothing coming back, which is exactly the pattern where Nagle plus the client's\r\ndelayed ACK stalls the sender: each frame waits for the previous one to be acknowledged, and the acknowledgement is\r\nheld back by the peer for up to 40 ms.\r\n\r\nMeasured with the Dynamo SGLang sidecar as the gRPC client (same host, loopback, Qwen3-0.6B, nightly `c10e0e17`,\r\nthree rounds), compared with the same deployment through the Rust server's `api.v1` listener and with the in-process\r\n`sgl.Engine` path:\r\n\r\n| | TTFT p50 at concurrency 1 | ITL p99 at concurrency 64 | inter-token gaps > 2× median, c=64 | gaps in the 36–44 ms band (of ≈162 k) |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| runtime.v1 gRPC server, as is | **46.6 ms** | **40.1 ms** | **10.7 %** | 5704 |\r\n| same, `TCP_NODELAY` forced on accepted sockets (`LD_PRELOAD` shim, nothing else changed) | 21.2 ms | 25.4 ms | 0.97 % | 492 |\r\n| Rust server (`api.v1`, already sets `TCP_NODELAY` in `utils/sock.rs`) | 22.0 ms | 22.9 ms | 0.84 % | 240 |\r\n| in-process `sgl.Engine` | 21.7 ms | 25.5 ms | 0.99 % | — |\r\n\r\nThroughput and the ITL median are unchanged by the option; only the first-token delay and the 40 ms tail go away.\r\nThe Rust server's listeners (`rust/sglang-server/src/utils/sock.rs`) and the Python HTTP server already run with\r\n`TCP_NODELAY`; this brings the `runtime.v1` listener in line.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n- `rust/sglang-grpc/src/server.rs`: wrap the listener in `tonic::transport::server::TcpIncoming` with\r\n  `with_nodelay(Some(true))` (new `grpc_incoming` helper) instead of a bare `TcpListenerStream`, so every accepted\r\n  connection gets `TCP_NODELAY`. No other behavior changes; `serve_with_incoming_shutdown` and the shutdown path are\r\n  the same.\r\n- `rust/sglang-grpc/src/server/tests.rs`: unit test that a connection accepted through `grpc_incoming` reports\r\n  `nodelay() == true`.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\nNot applicable (transport-only change, no effect on model outputs).\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\nSee the table above. Raw runs: three rounds of the unmodified server vs. one run with the option forced, 64 requests\r\nat concurrency 1 and 640 at concurrency 64, ISL ≈1080 / OSL 256, `--stream-interval 1`; per-token latencies taken\r\nfrom the client's raw samples.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\r\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\r\n---\r\n### CI States\r\n\r\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40958267190](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40958267190)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40958267154](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40958267154)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\r\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
